00:16.820 --> 00:18.560
or the places where they're, like, forced to run.

00:18.920 --> 00:22.940
So you just map the red lights, the turnstiles, maybe the really steep downhill slopes.

00:23.040 --> 00:24.280
It sounds totally impossible.

00:24.620 --> 00:27.540
Right, a map of constraints instead of a map of actual things.

00:27.540 --> 00:34.580
But a groundbreaking new research paper argues that this completely bizarre, inverted map

00:34.580 --> 00:40.080
is exactly how the most advanced artificial intelligence on the planet views our reality.

00:40.440 --> 00:44.620
Yeah, and honestly, it might be how we view reality, too, without even really knowing it.

